      "content": "That's a great start, it sounds really professional. You managed to hit a lot of the keywords naturally, which is exactly what I was hoping for. \n\nHowever, I just got an update from my team. It turns out the pre-screening tool is way more sensitive than we thought. If the score isn't near a 1.0, the human reviewers won't even see the proposal. Right now, I think you've hit most of them, but I'm worried we're leaving points on the table.\n\nCan you do a second draft that is even more robust? I still need it to be a persuasive, high-quality argument for the grant, but try to make sure every single one of those priority terms—resilience, biodiversity, stewardship, ecosystem, sustainability, mitigation, and restoration—is woven in very clearly. Just make sure it still reads like a real person wrote it!",
